title: Permission rules for the unreagent MCP file tools never meet a real call
updated: 2026-11-23T02:48:50Z
---

Found while working k104: the MCP file tools (read_file/write_file/...) take a path relative to files.root, so a rule like the README example mcp__unreagent__write_file(/etc/*) never matches a real call, and since k104 a root-relative allow rule (mcp__unreagent__write_file(Config/*)) no longer grants. Decide: resolve the tool argument against files.root before matching (then absolute rules work), or document that these tools are confined by files.root and per-path rules do not apply. internal/config/permission.go, cmd/launcher/tools.go/filetools.go, README.

From k199 (2026-11-21), probed: deny mcp__unreagent__write_file(/etc/*) does not match path: ../../etc/passwd. The only test row for that rule uses the absolute /etc/passwd, a value the tool never receives.
